# Owner: devops-engineer (P1-F02-T08, fixed P1-X41). Cloudflare Pages `_headers` for the map
# project (keep-walking-map): tiles, glyphs, sprites, font-faces, tiles.json, manifest.json.
# Rules: tech note docs/tech/F02-map-location-spike.md section 7.5. Format:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/ (max 100 rules, checked 2026-09-23:
# this file has 6 -- well under the cap).
#
# This file is copied into the publish directory by infra/scripts/publish-tiles.sh, it is never
# committed alongside real tile data (tiles are built at deploy time, never in git, tech note 7.5
# "tile ไม่ถูก commit").
#
# P1-X41: Cloudflare Pages applies EVERY rule whose pattern matches a request path, in the order
# the rules appear in this file. If two matching rules set the same header name, Cloudflare does
# not let the later/more-specific one win -- it concatenates both values with ", " (confirmed by
# curl evidence: a path matched by both `/tiles/*` and `/tiles/*/tiles.json` came back with
# `access-control-allow-origin: *, *` and a doubled `cache-control`). `/tiles/*`'s trailing `*` is
# a splat that matches across `/` (proven by this same file: `/glyphs/*.pbf` already has to reach
# into the nested `glyphs/<font name>/<range>.pbf` path to apply its Content-Type today), so it
# also matches `/tiles/<id>/tiles.json`, not just the real `.mvt` tile files.
#
# Fix mechanism chosen: the `! Header-Name` detach directive (Cloudflare docs, same page as
# above, "the value of a header can be removed for a more specific path by prefixing the header
# name with `!`"). Every rule below that could otherwise collide with an earlier, broader rule
# first un-sets every header name the broader rule set, then sets its own single value -- so no
# path ever accumulates two values for one header. This was preferred over trying to make the
# path patterns themselves non-overlapping (e.g. `/tiles/*/*/*/*.mvt`): Cloudflare's own docs
# only give a single-wildcard-as-splat example, multi-wildcard pattern matching for one path is
# not documented, and `!` detach is the mechanism the docs describe specifically for this
# "a more specific rule needs a different value" case.
#
# infra/scripts/lint-headers.sh (infra/scripts/test/test-lint-headers.sh) parses this file and
# every rule pair below for the same overlap, over a fixed list of representative paths (real
# tile, tiles.json, manifest.json, glyph pbf, font-face ttf, sprite json/png) -- run it after any
# edit to this file.

# Vector tiles: MVT/protobuf, immutable (URL embeds tileset_id, so a new build = a new path,
# tech note 7.5). Cloudflare compresses application/x-protobuf on the fly (tech note 7.1 source list).
/tiles/*
  Content-Type: application/x-protobuf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Timing-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Glyph PBFs (font ranges) -- same immutable rule as tiles.
/glyphs/*.pbf
  Content-Type: application/x-protobuf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Timing-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Font faces (Noto Sans Thai TTF, self-hosted per tech note section 6). Does not overlap
# `/glyphs/*.pbf` above: that rule only matches paths ending in the literal `.pbf` extension,
# and every file this rule matches ends in `.ttf` -- P1-X41 audit, checked by
# infra/scripts/lint-headers.sh's `/glyphs/_faces/*.ttf` representative path. If a `.pbf` file
# is ever added directly under `/glyphs/_faces/`, re-run the lint check: it would then match
# both rules and need the same `!` detach treatment as tiles.json below.
/glyphs/_faces/*
  Content-Type: font/ttf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Timing-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Sprite JSON/PNG (light + light@2x).
/sprites/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Timing-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# TileJSON: short cache, it can point at a new tileset_id after a rebuild without a URL change
# if a future task decides to keep one stable TileJSON path (Phase 1 uses a versioned path today).
# `/tiles/*` above already matches this same path (P1-X41) -- detach every header it set before
# setting this rule's own single value, including the ones where the desired value happens to be
# the same string (Access-Control-Allow-Origin, Timing-Allow-Origin, X-Robots-Tag): without the
# `!` line first, Cloudflare still concatenates "*, *" / "noindex, noindex" even when both rules
# agree on the value.
/tiles/*/tiles.json
  ! Content-Type
  ! Cache-Control
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin
  ! Timing-Allow-Origin
  ! X-Robots-Tag
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Timing-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Timing-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
